<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>What Is an Orange Julius?</h2>
  <p>The Orange Julius predates Dairy Queen by 14 years — it was first created in 1926 in Los Angeles, California. The original recipe blended orange juice with a proprietary creamy powder base that created a smooth, frothy, almost milkshake-like texture without dairy. International Dairy Queen, Inc. acquired the Orange Julius brand, which is why you find it at select DQ and combined DQ/Orange Julius locations. Find all DQ drink options on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

  <h2>Orange Julius vs. Fresh Orange Juice</h2>
  <p>An Orange Julius is not just orange juice. The "Julius" base is what makes it different — a proprietary blend that creates a light, frothy, creamy foam throughout the drink. The result is significantly smoother and lighter-tasting than straight OJ, with a subtle sweetness and an almost airy texture. Think of it as the frozen dessert world's version of an orange creamsicle in beverage form.</p>

  <h2>Orange Julius Flavors Available</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Flavor</th><th>Small Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Original Orange Julius</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>~210</td><td>Classic OJ with the Julius creamy base</td></tr><tr><td>Strawberry Banana Julius</td><td class="price-cell">$4.29</td><td>~230</td><td>Strawberry + banana + Julius base</td></tr><tr><td>Tropical Julius (seasonal)</td><td class="price-cell">$4.29</td><td>~240</td><td>Tropical fruit blend + Julius base</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

  <h2>Availability — Important Note</h2>
  <p>The Orange Julius is available at DQ/Orange Julius combination locations and some standalone Orange Julius stores. Most standard DQ locations do not carry Orange Julius. Use the official DQ location finder or the DQ app to find your nearest DQ/Orange Julius location before making a special trip.</p>

